---

<h2 id="trigger" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">1. Trigger phrase</h2>

When the user says something like:

> Following the **basicprac** rule, user will fill/select the `<user_input_cols>`, and copy over the `<other_shown_cols>` from the corresponding grid under the Basic knowledge chip.

…implement a **Basic practice** page/grid for that knowledge area using this recipe. Do **not** invent a one-off MUI table with a Result column and a Check button.

---

<h2 id="chrome" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">2. Shared chrome (required)</h2>

Reuse these modules under `apps/web/src/components/practice/` and helpers:

| Piece | Module | Role |
|-------|--------|------|
| Table chrome | `PracticeGroupedTable` | Centrally applies `learn-grouped-table` + blue `learn-table-head-*`; do not rebuild a raw MUI `<Table>` header per page |
| Article picker | `PracticeArticleToggle` | o \| a \| optional — |
| Inline feedback | `PracticeInlineGrade` | ✓ / ✗ expected / not yet done |
| Round banner | `PracticeRoundSummary` + `summarizePracticeRound` | N / M · K not yet done |
| Footer | `PracticeGridActions` | Submit + Clear All + Back to basic knowledge |
| Dirty state | `useBasicPracticeWorkbench` (+ `basicPracticeSession`) | Workbench checkpoint for drafts/grades; same dirty-submit API as `usePracticeDirtyAnswers` (memory-only helper for tests) |
| Dense CSS | class `basic-practice-grid` on the page/grid root | Toggle/input density |
| **Row colors** | Same `groupKey` / `groupOrder` as Basic knowledge via `annotateGroupedRows`; render with `practiceGroupedRowClass(row, idx)` | The annotator emits **`groupClass`** (not `rowClassName`); never zebra by row index |

Reference exemplars: `ArticleWordPracticeGrid`, `NounSpellPracticeGrid`, `PlacesPracticePage`, `NumbersPracticePage`.
Places grouping: `apps/web/src/lib/placesGrouping.ts` (shared by knowledge + practice).

---

<h2 id="columns" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">3. Column contract</h2>

1. Open the matching **Basic knowledge** grid for the same chip/tab.
2. **`user_input_cols`** — columns the learner fills or selects (Article toggle, Form text, Masculine/Feminine, …). Put these **left**; attach `PracticeInlineGrade` beside each control.
3. **`other_shown_cols`** — cue columns copied from knowledge (Word, Place, Rank, Number, Practice note, …). Show as read-only; accent the primary cue with `learn-table-cell--accent`.
4. Drop knowledge-only columns (Note, Grouping Note, Example, Translation, …) unless the user explicitly names them in `other_shown_cols`.
5. Keep the **same row set and order** as Basic knowledge (reuse knowledge builders / sort helpers when they exist).
6. **Row tinting:** reuse the knowledge grid’s Grouping Note `groupKey` + `groupOrder` so practice bands match knowledge colors (see Places `placesGrouping`).
7. **Header tinting:** render through `PracticeGroupedTable`. Tests must assert `learn-grouped-table` on the table and `learn-table-head-cell` on every column header; visual similarity by default MUI theme is not sufficient.

---

<h2 id="behavior" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. Behavior contract</h2>

- Blank cells stay **not yet done** after Submit (do not mark incorrect).
- **Submit** (not “Check”); disable when nothing dirty/new to grade.
- **Clear All** resets answers + grades (and saves empty Workbench checkpoint); do **not** call `resetAll()` inside row `load()` — that wiped restored grades.
- Drafts + ✓/✗ persist via Workbench keys `basic_<area>_<scope>` (separate from paragraph / `conj_matrix`). Profile stats still bump only on Submit → `record_attempt`.
- **Back to basic knowledge** links to the matching knowledge path.
- Multi-field rows: one dirty id per fillable cell (`id::masc`, `id::fem`, …); pass `field` on API submit.
- **Always** register a `ContentSpec` in `apps/api/app/services/practice_content_registry.py` and submit via `submitGenderPractice` (or the area’s submit helper) so the API hits centralized **`record_attempt`** (non-conj lemma stats: durable `content_key` + `display_label`, `practice_kind=basic`). Local-only UI grading is not enough for new areas.
- Send the backend's **canonical mode** from the client (a key already present in `MODE_CONTENT_TYPE`, e.g. `adjective_pairs`). A route/chip alias may also be registered in `CHIP_MODE_MAP`, but must not be the client's only working mode: a still-running pre-alias API process otherwise returns `400 Unknown practice mode`.

